1
00:00:00,219 --> 00:00:05,016
Centuries later, Athens ruled that no
one could be born on Delos, or die there.

2
00:00:05,016 --> 00:00:09,096
Leto was pregnant with Zeus's twins,
and Hera hunted her across the earth.

3
00:00:09,173 --> 00:00:13,240
Land after land turned her away;
none dared let her give birth.

4
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:16,008
At last she reached
Delos — a bare rock that,

5
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:18,533
in some tellings,
floated loose on the sea.

6
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:22,981
Even Delos was afraid the god would
despise it and kick it into the waves.

7
00:00:23,187 --> 00:00:27,528
So Leto swore an oath: his temple
would make Delos rich forever.

8
00:00:27,645 --> 00:00:31,580
Leto threw her arms around a palm
tree, the earth laughed beneath her,

9
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:34,281
and the child sprang out into the light.

10
00:00:34,281 --> 00:00:35,366
It was Apollo.

11
00:00:35,382 --> 00:00:39,908
The whole island blossomed with gold,
and the newborn god spoke at once.

12
00:00:39,908 --> 00:00:42,203
The one land that let
Leto give birth became

13
00:00:42,203 --> 00:00:45,003
the one place in Greece
where nobody could.
